  "description": [
    "Socketed Teensy 4.1 (on-board DP83825 Ethernet PHY) and its expansion,",
    "service and test interfaces. Teensy VUSB/VIN are not fitted on the carrier",
    "(power enters via the internal USB-A -> micro-B cable per power-usb).",
    "Cross-sheet nets (rails, SPDIF, ETH_*, PATH_SELECT, TX_ENABLE) are global",
    "labels consumed by the optical-spdif and ethernet sheets; see nets.md and",
    "pin-map.md."
  ],
  "design_notes": {
    "ethernet_phy": "The DP83825 PHY is ON the Teensy 4.1 (order the 'with Ethernet chip' variant). The 6-pin native-Ethernet header carries MDI differential pairs (ETH_RX+/-, ETH_TX+/-) + LED to the magjack on the ethernet sheet - NOT RMII to an external PHY. The PJRC Ethernet Kit is only a magjack + centre-tap cap + ribbon, no PHY. No DP83825 on the carrier.",
    "power_entry": "VIN and VUSB are no-connect: the Teensy is powered through its own micro-B jack from the internal USB-A cable (power-usb sheet), the sole 5V feed. No second VIN/VUSB feed.",
    "safe_defaults": "R17 pulls PATH_SELECT low (processed path) and R18 pulls TX_ENABLE low (optical TX disabled) - the hardware-safe optical defaults from interfaces-and-states, held before firmware runs.",
    "expansion_3v3": "expansion-3v3 == teensy-3v3 (+3V3). Per-signal protection is the design's backfeed guard: TCA9517A isolator on I2C, 1k series clamps on SPI/UART/I2S/GPIO-ADC exported CMOS signals. The one expansion reverse-blocking power switch (TPS2553 U12) guards the USB-host VBUS domain (protected-5V source). See nets.md for the one-switch resolution of the interface's two protected expansion domains.",
    "i2c_isolator": "TCA9517A: A-side (pins 2/3) to Teensy SCL0/SDA0 (pin 19/18) with 4.7k pull-ups to +3V3; B-side (pins 6/5) to J10 with 4.7k pull-ups to +3V3. EN (pin1) tied high.",
    "usb_host_switch": "TPS2553 U12: IN=VBUS_5V, OUT=EXP_USBH_VBUS (feeds Teensy USBH_5V pad and J14 VBUS). EN pulled to +3V3 (enabled while core powered, off when core unpowered = safe). ILIM ~0.5A. Note: the BOM lists one expansion TPS2553; it is assigned here to the USB-host VBUS domain.",
    "led_pin13": "Pin 13 is the Teensy on-board LED (shared with SCK0); it is reserved, not routed on the carrier (no-connect). SPI uses SPI1 (SCK1=27/MOSI1=26/MISO1=1/CS1=38) so pin 13 serves the LED only - no pad serves two functions.",
    "tag_connect": "TC2030-IDC bring-up point taps +3V3, GND, PROGRAM, ON_OFF and the debug UART (shared net with J12) - same function at two access points, not a second function on one pad."
  },
